WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:19.841
"Glumdalclitch and Grildig," the king said one day, "we are going to a town near the south coast."

2
00:00:19.842 --> 00:00:22.843
"That's wonderful," I replied.

3
00:00:22.844 --> 00:00:25.078
"I'd like to see the sea again."

4
00:00:25.079 --> 00:00:28.071
We reached the town a few days later.

5
00:00:28.072 --> 00:00:31.084
The next morning Glumdalclitch said to me,

6
00:00:31.085 --> 00:00:33.686
"I'm not feeling well.

7
00:00:33.687 --> 00:00:38.033
One of the queen's servants will look after you today."

8
00:00:38.034 --> 00:00:40.892
I asked the servant to take me to the sea.

9
00:00:40.893 --> 00:00:45.709
He carried me in my traveling box to a cliff above the shore.

10
00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:47.880
"I'll be back in half an hour,"

11
00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:50.860
he said, and went to look for birds' eggs.

12
00:00:50.861 --> 00:00:55.896
The day was warm and I fell asleep in my box, listening to the waves.

13
00:00:55.897 --> 00:01:01.133
I woke up because my box was moving and I was being thrown around inside it.

14
00:01:01.134 --> 00:01:03.572
I was very afraid.

15
00:01:03.573 --> 00:01:10.933
I could feel the box rising high up into the air, but I could not understand why that was happening.

16
00:01:10.934 --> 00:01:14.241
Soon the land and sea were far below me.

17
00:01:14.242 --> 00:01:20.039
I could hear a noise over my head that sounded like the flapping of a bird's wings.

18
00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:24.759
A large bird had picked up my box and was flying away with it!

19
00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:27.337
Suddenly, the bird dropped the box.

20
00:01:27.338 --> 00:01:30.687
With a loud splash, it hit the water.

21
00:01:30.688 --> 00:01:34.113
Luckily, the windows were shut and kept the water out.

22
00:01:34.114 --> 00:01:38.545
I was terrified because I could not get out of the box.

23
00:01:38.546 --> 00:01:40.692
Then I heard a clanking noise.

24
00:01:40.693 --> 00:01:43.906
My box now seemed to be moving through the waves.

25
00:01:43.907 --> 00:01:46.474
In front of me I could see a ship.

26
00:01:46.475 --> 00:01:50.480
Sailors from the ship had attached a heavy chain to my box.

27
00:01:50.481 --> 00:01:53.003
The ship was towing my box!

28
00:01:53.004 --> 00:01:57.395
"Help! Help!" I shouted loudly.

29
00:01:57.396 --> 00:01:59.774
I had to make the sailors hear me.

30
00:01:59.775 --> 00:02:03.130
I banged on the wall with my sword as I shouted.

31
00:02:03.131 --> 00:02:06.043
"Who are you?" a voice called out.

32
00:02:06.044 --> 00:02:09.362
"I'm Gulliver from England," I cried.

33
00:02:09.363 --> 00:02:11.921
"Please lift the box onto your ship."

34
00:02:11.922 --> 00:02:13.453
I heard laughter.

35
00:02:13.454 --> 00:02:19.759
Someone said, "Even ten men could not lift that box.

36
00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.288
He must be crazy!

37
00:02:21.289 --> 00:02:23.231
Let's see who's inside."

38
00:02:23.232 --> 00:02:26.833
A sailor cut a hole in the lid of my box.

39
00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:32.055
"You saved my life!" I said when I climbed out. "Thank you!"

40
00:02:32.056 --> 00:02:36.209
I was stunned to see that the sailors were my size.

41
00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:40.656
They asked me many questions and looked at all the things in my box.

42
00:02:40.657 --> 00:02:45.588
A tall man said to me, "Welcome to my ship, the Good Fortune.

43
00:02:45.589 --> 00:02:47.108
I am the captain.

44
00:02:47.109 --> 00:02:49.741
We are on our way home to England."

45
00:02:49.742 --> 00:02:56.934
"Captain," I said, "I thought I would soon die and never see England or my family again."

46
00:02:56.935 --> 00:03:00.362
"Why were you locked in that box?" he asked.

47
00:03:00.363 --> 00:03:02.746
"Why was it in the sea?"

48
00:03:02.747 --> 00:03:10.281
I told him the whole story—about my voyage on the Adventure and meeting the giants of Brobdingnag.

49
00:03:10.282 --> 00:03:12.533
About Glumdalclitch and the farmer.

50
00:03:12.534 --> 00:03:14.480
About living in the palace.

51
00:03:14.481 --> 00:03:16.676
About my traveling box.

52
00:03:16.677 --> 00:03:26.448
"And I fell asleep in my box on the cliff," I said, "and a huge bird grabbed it, then dropped it in the sea."

53
00:03:26.449 --> 00:03:29.711
"Get some sleep now," the captain said.

54
00:03:29.712 --> 00:03:32.499
I could tell he did not believe my story.

55
00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:35.363
Later I told him more about Brobdingnag.

56
00:03:35.364 --> 00:03:41.453
I showed him everything in my box, including the huge stingers from the bees I had killed.

57
00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:45.103
When he saw them, he finally believed me.

58
00:03:45.104 --> 00:03:51.348
"I have traveled far," he said, "but I have never seen a land of giants.

59
00:03:51.349 --> 00:03:54.731
How strange and wonderful the world is!"

60
00:03:54.732 --> 00:04:00.139
Months later, in June of 1706, the Good Fortune reached England.

61
00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:03.471
My family was very happy to see me.

62
00:04:03.472 --> 00:04:06.738
They were amazed when I described my adventures.

63
00:04:06.739 --> 00:04:13.285
"You must promise me," said my wife, "that you will never go to sea again."

64
00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:24.838
For now, my adventures had come to an end.
